t=1 setup: hostile blind referee, claim = 8E control-bug analysis (2^{+s} Mellin factor, zeros at Re=-(1/2+d), even-subsystem containment, control2 corrected). Read tools/wave8e/src/main.rs (512 lines) + note wave8e-control-direction-2026-08-18.md.
t=2 hand math: M[{a/(kx)}](s) = (a/k)^s * int_{a/k}^inf {u} u^{-s-1} du. Exact split: = (a/k)^s*(-zeta(s)/s) + (a/k)/(1-s). So {2/(kx)} factor 2^{+s}, {1/(2kx)}=Lambda_{2k} factor 2^{-s}. CONFIRMED by hand. 1+c0*2^s=0 -> s=-(1/2+d)+i pi(2m+1)/ln2 (Re=-0.6). 1+c0*2^{-s}=0 -> s=1/2+d +/- i pi/ln2 (0.6+4.532i). Both confirmed.
t=3 even-subsystem: {2/(2mx)}={1/(mx)} TRUE for the {2/(kx)} family. BUT control is the SUM family Lambda_k + c0{2/(kx)}; N=2 linear-independence argument shows span{control} does NOT contain Lambda_2 (contradiction unless {2/x} in span{L1,L2}, false: {2/x} breaks at x=2/n not 1/m). So "control span contains real span" is FALSE. Density of control span holds instead via symbol: (1+c0*2^s) bounded above and |1+c0*2^s| >= |c0*2^s|-1 >= 2^1.1-1 = 1.14 in Re(s)>1/2, zero-free -> dense under RH -> d_N -> 0 (Baez-Duarte structure preserved).
t=4 control2 saturation PROVEN: obstruction functional ell(f)=M[f](rho), rho=0.6+4.532i, bounded on L^2 (2beta-1=0.2>0), ell(Lambda''_k)=0 all k, ell(1)=1/rho != 0 => d''^2(N) >= (2beta-1)/|rho|^2 = 0.2/20.9 = 9.6e-3 > 0 for ALL N. Real d^2 -> 0 under RH. Discriminator correct in the limit. Also d''^2(60) >= real d^2(120) ~ 9.7e-3 (inclusion).
